  "steps": [
    "To a pot of boiling water add 60g raw soya chunks, 1 tsp salt.",
    "Once softened, drain and squeeze out all the excess water.",
    "Now to a bowl add the boiled soya chunks, 1 green bell pepper, roughly chopped, 1 onion, roughly chopped, 1 tomato, roughly chopped, 4 tbsp yogurt, 2 tbsp chickpea flour (besan), 1 tbsp ginger garlic paste, 1 tsp Kashmiri red chilli powder, ½ tsp turmeric powder, 1 tsp coriander powder, ½ tsp cumin powder, 1 tsp garam masala, ½ tsp black pepper, 1 tsp chaat masala, 1 tsp salt.",
    "Now add 1 tbsp hot mustard oil, 1 tsp dried fenugreek leaves and squeeze in half a lime.",
    "Mix everything really well until nicely coated and set aside.",
    "To a pan on medium heat add 1 tsp oil, toss in the marinated soya mixture and cook for 5 minutes until nicely roasted. Remove and set aside.",
    "To the same pan add: 1 tsp oil, 1 tsp cumin seeds, 1 finely chopped onion, 1 tsp Kashmiri red chilli powder, ½ tsp turmeric powder, 1 tsp coriander powder, ½ tsp salt, 1 cup tomato puree.",
    "Mix well and cook for 3 minutes or until the oil starts to separate.",
    "Now toss in the cooked soya mixture, add 150ml water and a handful of fresh coriander.",
    "Give everything a final mix, cook for another minute and it’s ready to serve!"
  ],
